1
00:00:08,742 --> 00:00:09,701
Hey,

2
00:00:13,664 --> 00:00:14,706
come eat with us.

3
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:22,773
It's hot, so I'll eat by the window
for some fresh air.

4
00:00:22,773 --> 00:00:23,799
Enjoy your food, guys.

5
00:00:23,799 --> 00:00:25,843
You know we're going hard
for afternoon practice, right?

6
00:00:25,843 --> 00:00:26,969
Got it.

7
00:00:27,511 --> 00:00:28,695
Dong Min,

8
00:00:28,695 --> 00:00:30,864
how's your wrist feeling after yesterday?

9
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:33,559
Yeah, the spray you gave me helped a lot.

10
00:00:33,559 --> 00:00:34,685
Thanks, UJU.

11
00:00:35,978 --> 00:00:37,229
Don't overdo it from now on,

12
00:00:37,229 --> 00:00:38,413
and let me know if you need more spray.

13
00:00:38,897 --> 00:00:39,731
Enjoy your food.

14
00:00:39,731 --> 00:00:40,691
Thanks.

15
00:00:43,652 --> 00:00:45,195
That's our captain.

16
00:00:45,195 --> 00:00:46,155
Look how thoughtful he is.

17
00:00:46,755 --> 00:00:50,325
I didn't even realize my wrist hurt in practice,

18
00:00:50,325 --> 00:00:52,661
so I'm glad UJU noticed.

19
00:00:53,328 --> 00:00:54,872
That's why he's the captain.

20
00:00:54,872 --> 00:00:56,373
He's great at volleyball too.

21
00:00:56,373 --> 00:00:57,958
I'm amazed every time we practice.

22
00:00:59,293 --> 00:01:00,460
Is he?

23
00:01:01,753 --> 00:01:04,715
HANBIN, haven't you ever thought
UJU was good?

24
00:01:04,715 --> 00:01:05,883
Nope.

25
00:01:05,883 --> 00:01:07,634
Pretty sure I'm better at volleyball.

26
00:01:08,969 --> 00:01:10,596
Well, you are good too, HANBIN.

27
00:01:13,515 --> 00:01:14,558
Guys,

28
00:01:15,225 --> 00:01:17,936
looks can be deceiving.

29
00:01:26,862 --> 00:01:28,197
Cool, my foot.

30
00:01:29,323 --> 00:01:31,408
You all need to room with him

31
00:01:31,408 --> 00:01:34,077
to see how exhausting he really is.

32
00:01:41,001 --> 00:01:43,462
This guy doesn't even need an alarm.

33
00:01:44,963 --> 00:01:47,566
He wakes up at the exact same time every day,

34
00:01:47,566 --> 00:01:49,067
like a living biological clock.

35
00:02:31,677 --> 00:02:33,262
What are you doing?

36
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,764
It's not time to get up yet.

37
00:02:36,765 --> 00:02:39,393
From what I saw last time,
you take a while to get ready.

38
00:02:40,102 --> 00:02:41,687
Get up now so you won't be late.

39
00:02:41,687 --> 00:02:42,729
Hurry up and get ready.

40
00:02:43,605 --> 00:02:44,856
Five more minutes...

41
00:02:52,030 --> 00:02:53,615
What are you doing?

42
00:03:16,388 --> 00:03:18,265
Why? Want some?

43
00:03:19,766 --> 00:03:21,435
You're dropping crumbs.

44
00:03:23,478 --> 00:03:24,605
Where?

45
00:03:25,105 --> 00:03:26,356
I didn't drop any.

46
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:28,483
It looks like you're about to.

47
00:03:40,996 --> 00:03:42,331
Put it there and eat.

48
00:03:42,331 --> 00:03:43,498
Don't make a mess.

49
00:03:44,333 --> 00:03:46,001
You even carry something like this around?

50
00:03:46,918 --> 00:03:48,086
It comes in handy.

51
00:03:48,086 --> 00:03:49,129
Thanks to someone.

52
00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:57,846
Even when I just eat a snack in the room,

53
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:00,641
he's already preparing to clean up.

54
00:04:08,148 --> 00:04:09,358
Hey.

55
00:04:10,275 --> 00:04:11,401
What?

56
00:04:11,401 --> 00:04:12,569
Turn down the brightness.

57
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:14,863
It's all the way down.

58
00:04:14,863 --> 00:04:16,590
You can't even see it from there anyway.

59
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,617
The light is leaking everywhere.

60
00:04:18,617 --> 00:04:19,634
I can feel it.

61
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:21,380
How much light could possibly leak?

62
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:22,454
Turn it down.

63
00:04:22,454 --> 00:04:24,514
He's the kind of guy who can't stand

64
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:26,375
even a single ray of light.

65
00:04:32,798 --> 00:04:34,925
I can barely see anything like this.

66
00:04:35,592 --> 00:04:36,927
Good.

67
00:04:36,927 --> 00:04:38,428
Then you can go to sleep too.

68
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:41,473
He's seriously...

69
00:04:42,891 --> 00:04:44,309
so annoying.

70
00:05:01,618 --> 00:05:03,762
Sure, I was the one who deliberately
wanted to share a room,

71
00:05:03,762 --> 00:05:05,664
and that's how we became roommates,

72
00:05:05,664 --> 00:05:07,457
but we're totally incompatible.

73
00:05:08,809 --> 00:05:11,311
Being assigned to the same room

74
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:12,796
was my plan from the start.

75
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:17,526
[Volleyball team room assignments]

76
00:05:17,526 --> 00:05:19,386
[HAN UJU, Kim Jin Young]

77
00:05:19,386 --> 00:05:20,862
[Room number: 201]

78
00:05:22,806 --> 00:05:24,783
I'm rooming with UJU.

79
00:05:24,783 --> 00:05:26,017
I'm doomed.

80
00:05:26,935 --> 00:05:27,911
Then...

81
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:29,855
Do you want to swap rooms with me?

82
00:05:30,605 --> 00:05:31,606
Huh?

83
00:05:31,606 --> 00:05:32,816
Sounds good, right?

84
00:05:34,484 --> 00:05:35,485
Uh, yeah.

85
00:05:38,238 --> 00:05:41,324
Because I needed a way
to stay close to him no matter what.

86
00:05:57,090 --> 00:05:58,091
What?

87
00:05:59,301 --> 00:06:00,427
Do you know me?

88
00:06:04,139 --> 00:06:06,641
Really? Hey, where's the coach's office?

89
00:06:07,225 --> 00:06:09,060
Hey, CHA SEJIN.

90
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,622
Long time no see.

91
00:06:13,164 --> 00:06:14,065
Did you just get here?

92
00:06:14,065 --> 00:06:15,358
Just got here.

93
00:06:15,942 --> 00:06:16,960
Alright.

94
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,111
I heard from your dad

95
00:06:18,111 --> 00:06:19,613
that you'd come here first.

96
00:06:20,739 --> 00:06:22,741
How was studying abroad?

97
00:06:22,741 --> 00:06:23,967
Shouldn't you rest a bit more?

98
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:26,536
I've rested enough.

99
00:06:28,079 --> 00:06:30,432
Let's go say hi to the team.

100
00:06:31,708 --> 00:06:33,168
Did you say hi to UJU?

101
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:36,254
HAN UJU is captain
of the volleyball team again.

102
00:06:41,843 --> 00:06:43,011
There he comes.

103
00:06:44,804 --> 00:06:45,805
Oh, UJU.

104
00:06:51,311 --> 00:06:52,562
Perfect timing.

105
00:06:53,313 --> 00:06:56,483
SEJIN is joining our team starting today.

106
00:06:56,483 --> 00:06:57,876
He just got here.

107
00:07:00,487 --> 00:07:01,696
Long time no see.

108
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:04,006
Yeah.

109
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:06,384
Right.

110
00:07:06,785 --> 00:07:09,704
It's really been a while for you two.

111
00:07:09,704 --> 00:07:10,914
Must be nice.

112
00:07:12,207 --> 00:07:15,043
SEJIN, let's talk for a bit—

113
00:07:20,507 --> 00:07:21,716
Oh, I have something urgent.

114
00:07:22,342 --> 00:07:23,885
Let me take this call...

115
00:07:23,885 --> 00:07:25,095
You two catch up.

116
00:07:25,095 --> 00:07:26,780
SEJIN, come by the coach's office later.

117
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:28,598
Yes, understood.

118
00:07:28,598 --> 00:07:29,699
Hello?

119
00:07:34,312 --> 00:07:35,272
Why are you here?

120
00:07:37,107 --> 00:07:38,275
To train.

121
00:07:39,818 --> 00:07:42,320
After leaving like that back then,

122
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:44,364
don't you think this is ridiculous?

123
00:07:45,907 --> 00:07:48,285
Whether I come back or not is up to me.

124
00:07:53,164 --> 00:07:54,416
You think volleyball is a joke?

125
00:07:55,917 --> 00:07:57,002
That's you.

126
00:07:58,503 --> 00:08:00,839
You look down on a lot of things
besides volleyball.

127
00:08:02,132 --> 00:08:03,008
What?

128
00:08:07,888 --> 00:08:09,014
Anyway,

129
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:10,557
I'm counting on you, Captain.

130
00:08:11,516 --> 00:08:13,518
Don't ignore me later,

131
00:08:14,019 --> 00:08:15,353
and take good care of me.

132
00:08:36,725 --> 00:08:38,627
He's completely different from the photos.

133
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:53,575
Shall We Start with a Foul?

134
00:08:54,434 --> 00:08:57,787
Joining our training starting today

135
00:08:57,787 --> 00:08:59,289
is trainee CHA SEJIN.

136
00:09:00,148 --> 00:09:03,418
He's a senior who studied abroad
in the US last year,

137
00:09:03,418 --> 00:09:06,921
and returned to Korea this year
to join our training.

138
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:09,591
[CHA SEJIN]

139
00:09:09,591 --> 00:09:10,592
[Outside hitter / 19 years old]

140
00:09:10,592 --> 00:09:11,551
[A powerful offensive asset back at SLA]

141
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:12,452
[A balanced wing spiker in offense and defense]

142
00:09:12,452 --> 00:09:13,511
[An all-rounder completing SLA's lineup]

143
00:09:14,763 --> 00:09:16,039
Everyone, give him a round of applause.

144
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,658
[Honor the court]

145
00:09:59,666 --> 00:10:01,309
I hate to admit it,

146
00:10:01,459 --> 00:10:02,877
but he's really good.

147
00:10:25,817 --> 00:10:27,085
CHA SEJIN.

148
00:10:27,085 --> 00:10:29,629
Let's focus, okay?

149
00:10:30,672 --> 00:10:32,006
Coach, my knee's acting up,

150
00:10:32,006 --> 00:10:33,324
could I take a short break?

151
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:37,220
Oh, sure.

152
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:38,429
Go ahead.

153
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:39,831
Thank you.

154
00:10:40,206 --> 00:10:43,460
If your knee hurts,
at least stand and do the basics.

155
00:10:43,460 --> 00:10:45,003
Standing is part of training too.

156
00:10:49,215 --> 00:10:51,009
Is the captain a doctor now?

157
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:54,054
All I asked was to rest my bad knee,
that's harsh.

158
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:57,515
If you don't want to do it, leave.

159
00:10:57,515 --> 00:10:58,808
The door is that way.

160
00:10:59,559 --> 00:11:00,685
Wait, wait, wait.

161
00:11:00,685 --> 00:11:01,686
CHA SEJIN.

162
00:11:02,312 --> 00:11:03,980
Coach, just a second.

163
00:11:05,340 --> 00:11:07,275
I'll say this one more time.

164
00:11:07,275 --> 00:11:08,985
Don't ruin the team vibe,

165
00:11:08,985 --> 00:11:10,278
and leave if you don't want to be here.

166
00:11:11,529 --> 00:11:12,655
Well,

167
00:11:13,531 --> 00:11:15,450
I don't see why I should.

168
00:11:16,868 --> 00:11:19,162
There's no point in trying hard anyway.

169
00:11:19,162 --> 00:11:21,289
You and I both know by now.

170
00:11:21,289 --> 00:11:23,541
The starting lineup is decided from the top.

171
00:11:28,505 --> 00:11:29,898
Right, Coach?

172
00:11:30,423 --> 00:11:32,108
Huh? No...

173
00:11:32,692 --> 00:11:34,260
No, SEJIN, that's...

174
00:11:40,016 --> 00:11:41,142
I'll go take a break.

175
00:11:48,024 --> 00:11:49,359
Back to practice.

176
00:11:58,368 --> 00:11:59,369
Bread!

177
00:12:12,132 --> 00:12:13,758
That's mine.

178
00:12:13,758 --> 00:12:14,843
I grabbed it first.

179
00:12:14,843 --> 00:12:16,219
I definitely grabbed it first.

180
00:12:19,264 --> 00:12:20,640
Hello, Coach.

181
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:23,893
There's no one there.

182
00:12:28,439 --> 00:12:29,816
You're the guy from earlier, right?

183
00:12:30,583 --> 00:12:31,568
Yeah, what about it?

184
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:34,946
Are you rooming with HAN UJU?

185
00:12:36,698 --> 00:12:37,866
Yeah.

186
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:42,453
Must be tough sharing a room with him.

187
00:12:43,221 --> 00:12:44,247
Not really.

188
00:12:46,457 --> 00:12:47,792
You're having that, right?

189
00:12:47,792 --> 00:12:48,835
Yeah.

190
00:13:00,805 --> 00:13:02,056
Ring this up, please.

191
00:13:03,892 --> 00:13:05,518
Thank you.

192
00:13:07,312 --> 00:13:08,271
Hey.

193
00:13:11,149 --> 00:13:12,150
Yeah?

194
00:13:14,110 --> 00:13:15,236
Eat before you go.

195
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:18,198
No thanks.

196
00:13:21,868 --> 00:13:23,244
Come on,

197
00:13:24,495 --> 00:13:26,539
we've got plenty of time.

198
00:13:27,415 --> 00:13:28,666
Just eat before you go.

199
00:13:29,584 --> 00:13:30,585
What's this about?

200
00:13:31,120 --> 00:13:32,395
Come on over.

201
00:13:32,395 --> 00:13:33,755
What is this?

202
00:13:49,228 --> 00:13:50,438
You're eating so well.

203
00:13:53,691 --> 00:13:55,526
Aren't you curious about UJU?

204
00:13:56,653 --> 00:13:58,529
Why would you ask that all of a sudden?

205
00:13:58,529 --> 00:13:59,739
No reason.

206
00:13:59,739 --> 00:14:02,116
I just know a lot about him.

207
00:14:02,116 --> 00:14:03,534
If you're curious, just ask.

208
00:14:07,163 --> 00:14:09,290
You messed with him on purpose today, right?

209
00:14:10,500 --> 00:14:11,542
What?

210
00:14:13,211 --> 00:14:14,145
My knee?

211
00:14:14,145 --> 00:14:15,672
My knee was actually hurting.

212
00:14:16,422 --> 00:14:17,482
It's bad.

213
00:14:19,467 --> 00:14:21,552
I know you two don't get along

214
00:14:22,387 --> 00:14:24,305
but don't ruin the vibe at practice.

215
00:14:25,890 --> 00:14:28,643
It's not fair to the guys working hard.

216
00:14:28,643 --> 00:14:29,936
Including me.

217
00:14:39,988 --> 00:14:41,364
You're funny.

218
00:14:43,157 --> 00:14:44,450
What's this all of a sudden?

219
00:14:44,993 --> 00:14:46,552
Hey.

220
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:48,037
Let's hang out more often.

221
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:51,666
I've been bored lately,
and you're pretty entertaining.

222
00:14:57,964 --> 00:14:59,607
Anyway, enjoy your food

223
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:01,050
and see you around.

224
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:18,026
What's his deal?

225
00:15:19,252 --> 00:15:21,504
[1st weekly training score sheet]

226
00:15:26,968 --> 00:15:28,678
They really posted it huge.

227
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,681
Of course UJU got an A.

228
00:15:31,681 --> 00:15:33,182
[SONG HANBIN]

229
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:34,142
I'm in trouble.

230
00:15:34,142 --> 00:15:35,268
[C]
I need to bring it up.

231
00:15:35,268 --> 00:15:37,019
I went up from a C to a B.

232
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:37,687
I'm so jealous.

233
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:41,524
My toss accuracy was definitely good yesterday

234
00:15:41,524 --> 00:15:43,885
and my receives were pretty solid too.

235
00:15:43,885 --> 00:15:45,344
How did this happen?

236
00:15:48,222 --> 00:15:51,100
And especially HAN UJU...

237
00:15:52,143 --> 00:15:54,145
He comes in late every night.

238
00:17:24,277 --> 00:17:26,529
Quietly sneaking in at the same time every day.

239
00:17:26,529 --> 00:17:28,239
Where does he even go?

240
00:17:42,378 --> 00:17:43,671
What are you doing here?

241
00:17:45,756 --> 00:17:47,008
What are you doing here?

242
00:17:49,385 --> 00:17:52,180
I'm pretty sure the gym is off-limits
at this hour.

243
00:17:55,641 --> 00:17:56,976
Didn't you hear on the first day?

244
00:17:56,976 --> 00:17:58,227
I'm in charge of the records.

245
00:17:59,145 --> 00:18:01,689
After practice,
organizing the sheets takes time

246
00:18:01,689 --> 00:18:03,191
so I come here to wrap it up.

247
00:18:03,191 --> 00:18:04,734
The coach knows about it too.

248
00:18:07,111 --> 00:18:08,237
I see.

249
00:18:10,198 --> 00:18:11,824
But...

250
00:18:11,824 --> 00:18:15,244
The other trainees
don't know about this, right?

251
00:18:26,047 --> 00:18:28,733
That the captain is in the gym
all by himself at this hour.

252
00:18:28,733 --> 00:18:32,820
Plus, regular trainees
aren't even allowed in the storage room

253
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,722
so going in and out of there...

254
00:18:35,598 --> 00:18:37,308
Wouldn't you be in trouble
if the others found out?

255
00:18:40,269 --> 00:18:41,729
What are you getting at?

256
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:46,484
I don't plan on telling anyone right now.

257
00:18:48,819 --> 00:18:50,696
Help me with my private training.

258
00:18:53,241 --> 00:18:54,116
What?

259
00:18:54,909 --> 00:18:56,494
Private training.

260
00:18:56,494 --> 00:18:58,120
I need to bring my score up.

261
00:18:59,372 --> 00:19:02,291
At this rate, I'm going to get cut.

262
00:19:02,291 --> 00:19:03,960
And I can't let that happen.

263
00:19:05,336 --> 00:19:07,380
If you coach me on the side,

264
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:10,007
I won't tell a soul about what I saw today.

265
00:19:11,467 --> 00:19:12,735
Are you blackmailing me right now?

266
00:19:12,735 --> 00:19:13,735
Come on.

267
00:19:15,054 --> 00:19:16,722
It's a deal. Just a trade.

268
00:19:19,183 --> 00:19:20,893
It's not a bad offer.

269
00:19:20,893 --> 00:19:22,395
I get to raise my score

270
00:19:22,395 --> 00:19:25,773
and of course, this stays
strictly between the two of us.

271
00:19:32,822 --> 00:19:35,074
Fine, deal.

272
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:39,203
But what about the ball noises
and the lights?

273
00:19:39,968 --> 00:19:43,124
Won't they get drowned out
when the soccer team plays?

274
00:19:47,169 --> 00:19:48,646
Right.

275
00:19:48,646 --> 00:19:49,814
Got it.

276
00:19:50,172 --> 00:19:52,400
Starting tomorrow, at this time.

277
00:19:52,675 --> 00:19:54,010
Make sure you keep your promise.

278
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:57,305
You better keep your mouth shut too.

279
00:19:58,340 --> 00:20:00,099
Of course.

280
00:20:03,102 --> 00:20:06,230
I didn't see a thing.

281
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:11,293
You really can't tell anyone
what you saw today.

282
00:20:13,571 --> 00:20:15,406
I'm not that kind of person.

283
00:20:33,674 --> 00:20:34,717
Pinky swear.

284
00:20:39,597 --> 00:20:42,116
Seriously, what do you take me for?

285
00:20:42,516 --> 00:20:44,727
Hurry up and pinky swear
while I'm asking nicely.

286
00:20:48,648 --> 00:20:50,791
There, happy?

287
00:20:52,318 --> 00:20:55,821
Our captain has way too many trust issues.

288
00:20:58,532 --> 00:21:01,202
Tomorrow at 9 PM. Don't be late.

289
00:21:02,203 --> 00:21:03,262
Got it.

290
00:21:06,582 --> 00:21:07,933
Hurry and go.

291
00:21:07,933 --> 00:21:09,143
I'm dead tired.

292
00:21:26,060 --> 00:21:27,978
Did I leave the record sheet over there?

293
00:21:53,671 --> 00:21:54,797
Is this barley tea?

294
00:22:01,095 --> 00:22:02,513
Something's weird...

295
00:22:05,474 --> 00:22:06,600
Whatever.

296
00:22:19,029 --> 00:22:20,614
I'm here.

297
00:22:22,658 --> 00:22:23,951
You're already here.

298
00:22:26,245 --> 00:22:27,371
UJU.

299
00:22:29,957 --> 00:22:31,125
UJU?

300
00:22:35,504 --> 00:22:36,797
What's wrong with your face?

301
00:22:37,631 --> 00:22:38,799
Are you okay?

302
00:22:39,550 --> 00:22:40,401
Huh?

303
00:22:41,552 --> 00:22:42,720
Yeah.

304
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:44,013
I'm fine.

305
00:22:45,306 --> 00:22:47,725
You don't look fine at all.

306
00:22:47,725 --> 00:22:50,661
Why? Is something wrong?

307
00:22:51,479 --> 00:22:52,438
Yeah.

308
00:22:53,981 --> 00:22:55,274
The taste is...

309
00:22:57,860 --> 00:22:59,195
weird.

310
00:23:00,738 --> 00:23:02,198
Let me see that.

311
00:23:14,043 --> 00:23:16,128
Did you just drink this?

312
00:23:16,128 --> 00:23:17,505
Do you even know what this is?

313
00:23:18,339 --> 00:23:20,633
What is it?

314
00:23:21,175 --> 00:23:22,885
It's alcohol. Alcohol!

315
00:23:22,885 --> 00:23:24,845
What were you thinking drinking this?

316
00:23:27,223 --> 00:23:28,557
It's a drink.

317
00:23:29,391 --> 00:23:31,185
Yeah, a drink.

318
00:23:34,355 --> 00:23:36,440
Looks like you drank quite a lot.

319
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:38,108
You're really something.

320
00:23:43,906 --> 00:23:46,408
Are you laughing right now?

321
00:23:46,408 --> 00:23:47,493
You're laughing?

322
00:23:48,744 --> 00:23:50,538
I'm sorry, but

323
00:23:50,538 --> 00:23:52,832
you're in pretty bad shape right now.

324
00:23:57,086 --> 00:23:58,337
I'm totally fine.

325
00:23:59,588 --> 00:24:01,465
Your face is completely red, though.

326
00:24:02,341 --> 00:24:03,551
It's always like this.

327
00:24:05,010 --> 00:24:06,595
Your eyes are glassy too.

328
00:24:13,644 --> 00:24:14,854
No, they're not.

329
00:24:25,281 --> 00:24:26,866
You're laughing again?

330
00:24:26,866 --> 00:24:28,576
You little...

331
00:24:28,576 --> 00:24:29,218
UJU.

332
00:24:45,693 --> 00:24:53,617
[Shall We Start with a Foul?]

333
00:24:53,617 --> 00:25:03,585
